    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">There might be some issue with how we&#39;re calling it from the python script then [we&#39;re not using PyStan], though I think I saw similar variations when I ran it straight from command line. It might be the seeds since I don&#39;t think we set them to anything particular, but I don&#39;t see why that would give so much variation in the warmup times. <div>\r\n\r\n<br></div><div>For instance, with the chains not in parallel from python script, here are the times [first column is warmup times and second column is sampling time]</div><div><br></div><div><div>0.783678  0.885639</div>\r\n<div>\r\n0.742387  0.83084</div><div>0.749547  0.86031</div><div>0.756207  0.838067</div><div>0.745775  0.842676</div><div>0.764761  0.850028</div><div>0.768055  0.839632</div><div>0.75288  0.870942</div><div>0.858897  0.944903</div>\r\n\r\n<div>0.809843  0.914556</div><div>0.804687  0.851096</div><div>0.766524  0.828348</div><div>0.746574  0.857063</div><div>0.749474  0.850166</div><div>0.742087  0.830808</div><div>0.798069  0.89224</div><div>0.742933  0.823869</div>\r\n\r\n<div>0.751209  0.858057</div><div>0.776687  0.84336</div><div>0.759792  0.842849</div></div><div><br></div><div>And with them in parallel: </div><div><br></div><div><div>0.597691  1.0708</div><div>0.713444  0.665822</div>\r\n\r\n<div>0.684196  0.665878</div><div>0.624916  1.04938</div><div>0.698641  0.718136</div><div>0.699391  0.833642</div><div>0.612821  0.791303</div><div>0.60912  0.668759</div><div>0.616617  0.674189</div><div>0.650921  0.704704</div>\r\n\r\n<div>0.596904  0.665802</div><div>0.624565  0.714502</div><div>0.614049  0.728062</div><div>0.588368  0.816542</div><div>0.615376  0.76874</div><div>0.597937  0.810229</div><div>0.652422  0.666215</div><div>0.689229  0.809552</div>\r\n\r\n<div>0.685087  0.778758</div><div>0.618826  0.684638</div><div>0.608461  0.663496</div><div>0.618216  0.714233</div><div>0.614835  0.771172</div><div>0.648977  0.834636</div><div>0.641712  0.711322