  {
   "id": "pJSYU9UmF8sJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2014-07-22T04:55:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-dev] Re: Running Chains in Parallel",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Monday, July 21, 2014 11:56:31 PM UTC-4, Peter Li wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">So if I run the model for 100 runs, 4 chains each, the 4 chains in each run should have the same seed, but from run to run they should have different seeds?</div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>Yeah, just make sure you specify the chain ID.<br><br>Ben<br><div><br></div>\n</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "RauQY2tP8XIJ",
   "from": "Michael Betancourt",
   "author": "a5e83218c834e013",
   "date": "2014-07-22T08:27:56Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-dev] Running Chains in Parallel",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>The chain id modifies the RNG so that parallel chains start with different seeds.  So when running in parallel this is okay,</div><div><br></div><div>seed=1 id=1</div><div>seed=1 id=2</div><div>seed=1 id=3</div><div>seed=1 id=4</div><div><br></div><div>but this is not,</div><div><br></div><div>seed=1 id=1</div><div>seed=1 id=1</div><div>seed=1 id=1</div><div>seed=1 id=1.</div><div><br></div><div>The former should be equivalent to something like,</div><div><br></div><div>seed=1</div><div>seed=2</div><div>seed=3</div><div>seed=4</div><div><br></div><div>and if it’s not then there’s something going wrong with the striding and the RNG.</div><br><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div>On Jul 22, 2014, at 5:55 AM, Ben Goodrich &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">goodri...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Monday, July 21, 2014 11:56:31 PM UTC-4, Peter Li wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">So if I run the model for 100 runs, 4 chains each, the 4 chains in each run should have the same seed, but from run to run they should have different seeds?</div></blockquote><div><br>Yeah, just make sure you specify the chain ID.<br><br>Ben<br><div><br></div>\r\n</div></div><div><br></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;stan development mailing list&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-dev+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474612261000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0o6mb3QKldOFfwNKb5s5qW\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div></div>"
